{% extends "base.html.jinja" %}
{% block content %}
<h1>{{ guide.h1 }}</h1>
<p class="lede">
  A plant is a delivery of catchable-size fish from a CDFW hatchery to a
  water. The schedule this site mirrors lists which waters CDFW plans to
  plant in which week.
</p>

<h2 id="meaning">What the words mean</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's <a href="{{ cdfw_schedule_url }}">Fish Planting Schedule</a> says the
  waters on it &ldquo;will be restocked with catchable-size fish from CDFW
  hatcheries,&rdquo; conditions permitting. CDFW calls the schedule a
  planting schedule and links a provisional stocking document from it, so
  &ldquo;plant&rdquo; and &ldquo;stocking&rdquo; are used for the same activity. This site
  says &ldquo;scheduled&rdquo; for every listing because a listing is a plan (see
  <a href="{{ root }}guide/scheduled-vs-confirmed/">scheduled vs. confirmed</a>).
</p>
<p>
  The name Trout Truck comes from what anglers call the hatchery truck that
  delivers planted trout. The site shows CDFW's weekly schedule, not where any
  truck is right now.
</p>

<h2 id="criteria">The limits CDFW sets for trout</h2>
<p>
  CDFW's page on
  <a href="{{ cdfw_criteria_url }}">temperature and flow criteria for planting
  catchable trout</a> says, in summary:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Streams</strong>: catchable trout are not planted when water
      temperatures reach 75&deg;F and are expected to keep reaching it, or when
      flows drop below 10 cfs. Streams with flows between 2 and 10 cfs may be
      planted if temperatures do not exceed 70&deg;F and other conditions are
      satisfactory. None are planted until afternoon temperatures reach
      45&deg;F or higher most days. Planting is discontinued if shallow water,
      lack of pools, algae growth or poor water quality make a stream
      unsuitable.</li>
  <li><strong>Lakes and reservoirs</strong>: not planted after surface
      temperatures reach 78&deg;F and are expected to keep reaching it, or after a
      die-off is attributed in whole or part to low oxygen, and not until
      afternoon temperatures reach 42&deg;F or higher most days. Planting may be
      suspended in reservoirs during spill. It is discontinued if algae
      blooms, weed growth, turbidity or alkalinity make a lake unsuitable.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  These criteria are for catchable trout. This site has not read a CDFW
  criteria page for any other species.
</p>

<h2 id="species">Species on this site</h2>
<p>
  Nearly every water on the schedule is trout; catfish are occasional. Each
  species has a page:
  {% for l in species_links %}<a href="{{ root }}species/{{ l.slug }}/">{{ l.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
</p>

<h2 id="where">Where plants are scheduled</h2>
<p>
  {{ water_count }} {{ "water is" if water_count == 1 else "waters are" }} in
  this site's record, across {{ county_counts|length }}
  {{ "county" if county_counts|length == 1 else "counties" }}. Browse by
  <a href="{{ root }}county/">county</a>, or by CDFW region:
  {% for r in region_links %}<a href="{{ root }}region/{{ r.slug }}/">{{ r.name }}</a>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
</p>

<h2>Keep reading</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/how-to-read-the-schedule/">How to read the schedule</a></li>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/scheduled-vs-confirmed/">Scheduled vs. confirmed</a></li>
  <li><a href="{{ root }}guide/">All guides</a></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="sources">Sources</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Quotations and criteria are from CDFW's
  <a href="{{ cdfw_schedule_url }}">Fish Planting Schedule</a> and
  <a href="{{ cdfw_criteria_url }}">Temperature and Flow Criteria for Planting
  Catchable Trout</a>, both fetched and read on {{ cdfw_read_on }}. Counts come
  from this site's own record. This site is independent and is not affiliated
  with CDFW.
</p>
{% endblock %}
